description:
Design a sign extension unit that takes a 16-bit immediate value and produces a 32-bit output based on the specified extension operation. The module selects one of three extension types based on the 2-bit ExtOp input: for ExtOp = 00, it sign-extends the 16-bit input; for ExtOp = 01, it zero-extends the 16-bit input by prepending 16 zeros; and for ExtOp = 10, it zero-extends by appending 16 zeros to the input.
module top_module(
    input [15:0] imm16,
    output reg [31:0] imm32,
    input [1:0] ExtOp
    );

code:
module top_module(
    input [15:0] imm16,
    output reg [31:0] imm32,
    input [1:0] ExtOp
    );always@*
	case(ExtOp)
		2'b00:	imm32=$signed(imm16);
		2'b01:	imm32={16'b0000_0000_0000_0000,imm16};
		2'b10:	imm32={imm16,16'b0000_0000_0000_0000};
	endcase
endmodule

