description:
Develop an adaptive equalizer using the Least Mean Squares (LMS) algorithm to improve signal fidelity. The module takes a distorted input signal and a reference signal, computes the error between them, and adjusts a set of coefficients (weights) accordingly. The output is the equalized signal, which is generated by multiplying the distorted signal by the updated weights. This architecture is aimed at optimizing signal quality in communication systems by dynamically adapting to variations in the input signals.
module top_module(
  input [n-1:0] dist_signal,
  input [n-1:0] ref_signal,
  output [n-1:0] eq_signal
);

code:
module top_module(
  input [n-1:0] dist_signal,
  input [n-1:0] ref_signal,
  output [n-1:0] eq_signal
);parameter n = 8; // number of input and output signals

reg [n-1:0] weights; // set of coefficients (weights)
reg [n-1:0] error; // difference between distorted and reference signals

// Least Mean Squares algorithm for adaptive equalization
always @(*) begin
  error = dist_signal - ref_signal;
  weights = weights - (error * dist_signal);
end

// Equalization circuit
assign eq_signal = dist_signal * weights;

endmodule

