description:
Design a frequency divider that generates a clock signal with a period of 10 milliseconds from a given input clock. The module counts the number of clock cycles from the input `clk`, and when the count reaches 500,000 (assuming a 50 MHz input clock), it toggles the output clock signal `clk_10ms`. The output clock `clk_10ms` will thus have a frequency that is 1/50th of the input clock frequency, providing a time base of 10 milliseconds.
module top_module(
   input clk,
   output reg clk_10ms   
   );

code:
module top_module(
   input clk,
   output reg clk_10ms   
   );reg [20:0]count=21'd0;
reg temp2=1'b0;
always @ (posedge clk)
if(count==21'd500000)
  begin
    temp2=~temp2;
    clk_10ms<=temp2;
    count<=21'd0;
  end  
else
  count<=count+1'b1;endmodule

