description:
Design a simple 32-bit counter that increments its value by 1 on each rising edge of a 50 MHz clock signal (CLOCK_50). The counter output (counter_out) holds the current count value, allowing for a maximum count of 2^32 - 1 before wrapping around back to zero. This module serves as a basic timing or frequency division element in digital circuits.
module top_module(
 CLOCK_50,
 counter_out
 );

code:
module top_module(
 CLOCK_50,
 counter_out
 );input CLOCK_50 ;
output [31:0] counter_out;
reg [31:0] counter_out;

always @ (posedge CLOCK_50) 
begin
counter_out <= #1 counter_out + 1;
end
endmodule

